### Graphify ###
# Knowledge-graph state. Regenerate with: graphify update .
.graphify/
# Pre-0.17 layout, kept so an unmigrated tree stays ignored (see graphify migrate-state)
graphify-out/
# Installed CLI. The pin and lockfile ARE tracked; restore with:
#   cd tools/graphify && npm install --ignore-scripts
tools/graphify/node_modules/

### OpenCode Goal Plugin ###
.opencode/goals/

### OpenCode nested config guard ###
# A nested .opencode/ dir is created when opencode runs with a cwd inside
# .opencode/. Its node_modules/*.md files get registered as phantom agents.
.opencode/**/.opencode/
### Elevation of Privilege deck sources ###
# The Illustrator/InDesign native sources for the printed cards and box are ~86 MB
# and are never used to build anything here — the deck content comes from cards.yaml.
# The PDFs in docs/EoP_Microsoft_Docs/ ARE tracked; this one archive is not, so the
# clone stays small. Re-download from Microsoft if the artwork is ever needed:
#   https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/download/details.aspx?id=20303
docs/EoP_Microsoft_Docs/EoP_Cards_Box_Native_files.zip

# k6 run artefacts. Every load-test run writes a timestamped JSON pair here, so the
# directory would grow without bound. docs/performance/TRENDS.md is the curated
# record; the raw runs are local evidence. The directory itself stays tracked via
# its .gitkeep.
docs/performance/history/*.json

# The k6 output directory used by the CI canary (EOP-155, ADR-055) and by any local
# run of the same step. CI collects it as the `k6-results` workflow artifact, which
# is deliberately where those numbers stop: a run on a shared 2-vCPU runner must
# never reach TRENDS.md, whose baseline was measured against the real topology.
test/k6/results/

### Build and run logs ###
# Redirected build or application output (`./mvnw ... > app.log`, `spring-boot:run`
# tee'd to a file). Machine-specific, regenerated on every run, and large — one
# such file was committed by accident during EOP-155, which is why this is a
# blanket pattern rather than a named path.
*.log

### Agent scratch space ###
# Throwaway working area for agents and humans: experiments, generated output,
# and `git worktree add .tmp/scratch HEAD` checkouts. Inside the worktree on
# purpose, so it needs no `external_directory` permission grant (blueprint §7.9).
# It MUST stay at the repository root. A scratch copy under docs/ or src/ would
# be walked by DeckArithmeticClaimsTest (Files.walk over docs/ and src/) and turn
# `./mvnw verify` red on duplicated prose.
.tmp/

# Python bytecode caches. tools/*.py are developer scripts run ad hoc, so CPython
# drops a __pycache__ beside them on any import or py_compile. The bytecode is
# machine- and interpreter-version-specific and regenerates on demand, so it is
# never worth reviewing in a diff.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Orphaned SonarQube report temporaries. tools/sonar/scan.sh writes the report to
# a mktemp sibling and renames it over the real file, so that a crash mid-write
# cannot leave the tracked sonar-report.json truncated (a plain `>` redirect
# truncates its target before the writing process even starts). Its EXIT trap
# removes the temporary on every signal a trap can catch, so this pattern only
# ever matches after a SIGKILL or a power loss - but when it does match, the
# stray is named like the report it protects, which is exactly the confusion the
# rename was introduced to remove. See ADR-060.
tools/sonar/sonar-report.json.*
